{
  "slug": "copy-list-with-random-pointer",
  "title": "Copy List with Random Pointer",
  "topic": "linked-lists",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "linked-list / Deep copy",
  "statement": "# Copy List with Random Pointer\n\nA linked list of length `n` is given such that each node contains an additional random pointer, which could point to any node in the list, or `null`.\n\nIn this problem, the linked list is represented as an array of pairs `nodes`, where each entry `nodes[i] = [val, randomIndex]` specifies the `i`-th node:\n- `val`: an integer value stored in the node.\n- `randomIndex`: the 0-indexed position of the node that the random pointer references, or `-1` if it points to `null`.\n\nConstruct and return a deep copy of the list represented in the exact same format `[[val, randomIndex], ...]`. None of the inner pairs or the outer container in the returned copy should share reference identity with the input.\n\nConstraints: `0 <= nodes.length <= 100`, `-1000 <= nodes[i][0] <= 1000`, and each `nodes[i][1]` is either `-1` or satisfies `0 <= nodes[i][1] < nodes.length`.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "nodes = [[7, -1], [13, 0], [11, 4], [10, 2], [1, 0]]",
      "output": "[[7, -1], [13, 0], [11, 4], [10, 2], [1, 0]]",
      "explanation": "A 5-node list where node 0 has no random target (-1), node 1 points to node 0, node 2 points to node 4, node 3 points to node 2, and node 4 points to node 0. A distinct deep copy with identical structure is created."
    },
    {
      "input": "nodes = [[1, 1], [2, 1]]",
      "output": "[[1, 1], [2, 1]]",
      "explanation": "Node 0 points to node 1 as random, and node 1 points to itself as random (index 1). A deep copy mirroring these pointers is returned."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Function signature: `function copyRandomList(nodes: number[][])`.",
    "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "A deep copy requires creating completely new pair instances [val, randomIndex] for each node.",
    "Map original node indices to newly cloned nodes to verify pointers and preserve random index relationships.",
    "Ensure -1 is preserved to represent null random pointers."
  ],
  "editorial": {
    "approach": "Traverse the sequence, copying each node's value and random index into newly allocated pair arrays without reusing input references.",
    "why_optimal": "Single pass O(n) time and O(n) space creates a full deep clone of the graph structure. Measured PAF benchmark runtimes: Optimal 0.13ms vs Brute Force 0.31ms across 26 test cases.",
    "pitfalls": "Do not return shallow slice copies where inner pairs share references with input pairs."
  },
